brombadc@HYDRA.ROSE-HULMAN.EDU (Dave Brombaugh) asked:

> Somehow or another, I always seem to end up with the aggravate monster
> intrinsic.  Now, what would be really neat is if I could get rid of it
> somehow.  Is there a way to do this?

Well, yes and no.  The information below is a repost, and should answer
your question(s).

------------------------------------------------------------------------

From the source code, I have obtained information on:
  cannibalism
  eating pets
  aggravating monsters

SPOILER ALERT


If you are human (regardless of your polymorph state) and you eat a
human corpse, all that happens is that you gain the aggravate monster
intrinsic.  You don't lose luck; you don't piss-off your god; etc. 

If you are an elf and eat an elf corpse, the same thing happens.

If you eat a dog or cat corpse, you gain the aggravate monster
intrinsic.  This does not mean everthing with a "d" symbol (jackels,
wolves, etc.) or a "f" symbol (tigers, jaguars, etc.); just dogs
(small dog, large dog, etc.) and cats (kittens, housecats, etc.). 

Similarly, human corpses do not originate from all things with the @
symbol.  Human corpses come from kops, soldiers, werecreatures, other
players (on bone levels), human zombies and mummies, nurses,
shopkeepers, guards, oracles, temple priests and priestesses and the
Wizard of Yendor. 

Elf corpses, obviously, come from elves, elf mummies and elf zombies.

The only thing the aggravate monster intrinsic does is cause sleeping
monsters to wake up when you enter the room.  However, since the code
checks for "stealth" (intrinsic or ring) first, having stealth will 
nullify the aggravate monster intrinsic.  This is much better and 
easier than trying to get a gremlin to "steal" the intrinsic.



